# Pairs with RecoveryNeverFallsOffLog. The GC retires the pin of a leaf that still
# has its row (a drive that misreports the tree id of a bound leaf), so it trims
# past the leaf's durable checkpoint and the leaf latches stale on its next
# activation. The base retires only a rowless leaf's pin, which never activates again
# without a create intent. With every pin retired the GC trims the whole bounded
# stream, which can exhaust the instance before any leaf restarts: DEADLOCK: off.
MODULE: RecoveryNeverFallsOffLogPinRetiredWhileRowLive
TARGET: RecoveryNeverFallsOffLog
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the GC retires a live leaf's pin and trims past its checkpoint
PERTURBS: PinRetire
DEADLOCK: off

--- FIND
    /\ ~row[l]
    /\ pinHlc[l] # "gone"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the pin of a leaf with a row is retired too.
    /\ pinHlc[l] # "gone"
--- END